{
  "_comment": [
    "Pre-registered paraphrase corpus for Feature 005 US1 (T044, SC-736).",
    "",
    "Fifty claim pairs, ten per knowledge kind. Each pair is one claim",
    "written two ways: `topic_a`/`topic_b` are two wordings of the same",
    "topic, and `value_a`/`value_b` are two wordings of the same value.",
    "Both wordings of each half MUST normalize (cairn_core::knowledge::",
    "normalize_topic_key / normalize_value_key) to the identical string \u2014",
    "that identity is exactly what makes a restatement reinforce instead",
    "of creating a second record (contracts/consolidation.md \u00a77).",
    "",
    "Every wording is deliberately a single shell-token / path-stem shape",
    "(hyphen, slash, case and doubled-separator variation; no bare space)",
    "because the representative subset of this corpus that",
    "`feature005_consolidation_restart.rs` drives through the real",
    "pipeline embeds these strings directly into a `test_command` and a",
    "`repo_file` for R1 (fix-confirmed-by-tests) \u2014 the one deterministic",
    "rule that derives its keys from free text rather than from a",
    "vocabulary-justified token, so it is the rule this corpus can drive",
    "end to end without also constructing session vocabulary.",
    "",
    "'variation' on each half names the separator-folding technique it",
    "exercises (contracts/extraction.md \u00a77): hyphen, case, slash, a",
    "doubled separator, and upper-case-plus-hyphen against a lower-case",
    "hyphen. Both sides of every pair are asserted to normalize identically",
    "in `feature005_consolidation_restart.rs`."
  ],
